name: Benefits and tax fraud
tagline: "A seeded benefits and tax fraud Link Analysis demo - an address farm, payments to the deceased, undeclared work and a tax-preparer ring, planted among 12 000 people, 7 500 claims and 8 000 tax returns with benign look-alikes"
description: "The benefits-integrity and tax-compliance Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Seven synthetic feeds (address, person, household, claim, death_register, payroll, tax_return; 12 months landed from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, the next month in data/staged; 12 000 people at about 5 250 of 6 500 addresses, about 7 500 claims, 300 deaths, about 36 000 payroll rows and 8 000 tax returns) are landed by seven Collectors and Pipelines. The benefits_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via) of six link kinds; the benefits_screen_links Job derives the four integrity screens the saved views read. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-benefits-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by BenefitsLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-benefits-data.test.mjs): 14 claimants under 5 surnames at one address, each declaring a household of one, paid into 3 accounts; 9 pensions still paid months after the deaths into 3 accounts that also take one living person's claims; 20 jobseekers on 2 employers' payroll at full wages; a tax preparer whose 80 clients' inflated refunds go to 6 accounts. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: 3 care homes, a death notified 40 days late with the overpayment recovered, a jobseeker with permitted earnings under the limit, and a large preparer whose clients are refunded into their own accounts. Four saved views. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: benefits.analyst lead, benefits.manager second approver, benefits.reviewer read-only, benefits.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the benefits_deceased_counts and benefits_deceased_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule benefits_paid_to_the_deceased_after_notice (a claim of a person on the death register still paid more than 30 days after the death was notified; on the shipped data it counts the 9 pensions, into 3 accounts that also take 3 claims of one living person, and never the death notified 40 days late or the 314 other claims stopped 0-5 days after their notice; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-benefits.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:banknotes
contents[7]: "7 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "benefits_links Job + Dataset (6 link kinds, via) and the benefits_screen_links Dataset of four integrity screens", "4 saved views (shared addresses, paid after death, work while claiming, refund concentration)", "4 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Ground truth and golden tests in the repository", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on payments to the deceased after the death notice (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
